# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sened environment configuration
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. Never commit real keys.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Legend
#   [server]  server-only secret or setting, read at RUNTIME via process.env.
#             Never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_ and never bake into an image.
#   [public]  NEXT_PUBLIC_*: inlined into the browser bundle at BUILD time by
#             `next build`. Changing it needs a rebuild; it is visible to every
#             visitor, so it must not be a secret.
#
# Every variable below is read by the code; nothing here is decorative. The
# `/api/*` routes and the providers are inert (fail closed) until configured.

# --- Supabase (required for any /api route and for sign-in) ----------------
# [public] + [server]. Read in src/lib/supabaseServer.ts (runtime, server) and
# src/lib/auth/browserClient.ts (build time, browser).
# Without these the API returns 503 not_configured and the browser treats the
# visitor as signed out, which is expected. The anon key is public by design:
# every /api route re-verifies the user's JWT itself. When building a container
# these two must be passed as build args (see Dockerfile and
# docs/DEPLOYMENT.md); setting them only on the running container fixes the
# server half but NOT the browser half.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Bank reference protection (required for /api/bank-verifications) ------
# [server] secrets. Read in src/lib/banking/vault.ts and service.ts.
# Provider references (receipt URLs / transaction ids) are sealed at rest with
# AES-256-GCM and authenticated with HMAC-SHA256. Both keys MUST be 32 bytes,
# base64 encoded. Generate a fresh pair per environment:
#
#   openssl rand -base64 32
#
# Rotating BANK_REFERENCE_ENCRYPTION_KEY makes existing sealed references
# unreadable, so plan a re-seal before rotating.
BANK_REFERENCE_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
BANK_REFERENCE_HMAC_KEY=
BANK_REFERENCE_KEY_VERSION=v1

# --- links.et receipt verification (required for M2.2 / M2.3) --------------
# [server] Read in src/lib/banking/linkset.ts.
# links.et (by Odit) fetches the receipt from the issuing Ethiopian bank over an
# Ethiopia-egress link and returns the bank's own record as JSON. It is a read
# service: it never moves money and never needs bank credentials.
#
# Docs:   https://links.et/docs
# Agents: https://links.et/agents.md
# Key:    minted at https://links.et/dashboard/keys (starts with `vk_`)
#
# This is a SERVER-SIDE credential. Never expose it as NEXT_PUBLIC_* and never
# call links.et from a browser.
#
# With no key the adapter reports itself unconfigured and every verification
# fails closed. It never fabricates a "verified" result.
LINKS_ET_API_KEY=

# Override only if you are self-hosting links.et or testing against a sandbox.
LINKS_ET_BASE_URL=https://links.et

# First-response budget in ms, sent as links.et's `waitMs` (max 30000).
# ROADMAP M2.2 asks for 800ms. An uncached receipt against a busy bank can hold
# the connection for up to ~120s, so when links.et answers `202 queued` we mark
# the intent PENDING_RECONCILIATION and the reconciliation queue resumes it.
LINKS_ET_WAIT_MS=800

# Hard ceiling on our own HTTP call. Must exceed LINKS_ET_WAIT_MS; the minimum
# enforced value is waitMs + 1000.
LINKS_ET_TIMEOUT_MS=5000

# Ethiopia Time is UTC+3, and bank receipts publish wall-clock times with no
# offset. Change only if a provider is observed to publish in another zone.
LINKS_ET_ETB_OFFSET_MINUTES=180

# Permitted clock skew between the treasurer's declared contribution time and
# the bank's own timestamp. This narrows ONLY the timestamp dimension; amount,
# currency, direction and both account fingerprints are always compared exactly.
LINKS_ET_TIMESTAMP_TOLERANCE_SECONDS=900

# --- Reconciliation drain (required to re-check PENDING_RECONCILIATION) -----
# [server] secrets. Read in src/lib/banking/reconciliationDrainRoute.ts.
# `POST /api/reconciliation/drain` re-checks verifications that links.et left
# pending (202 queued / timeout / rate limit). It is meant to be called by a
# scheduler, never by a user; see docs/DEPLOYMENT.md "Scheduling the
# reconciliation drain". Until BOTH secrets are set it returns 503 and does
# nothing, so pending verifications stay pending.
#
# Shared secret the scheduler sends as `Authorization: Bearer <secret>`. At
# least 32 characters; generate with:  openssl rand -base64 32
RECONCILIATION_CRON_SECRET=

# Supabase SERVICE-ROLE key (Settings > API). The queue RPCs are granted to the
# service role only and a cron has no user session. This key bypasses RLS: it is
# a SERVER-SIDE secret, used by the drain route and nothing else. Never expose
# it as NEXT_PUBLIC_*, never pass it as a build arg, never send it to a browser.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Per-call bounds so one invocation cannot outlive a serverless timeout.
# Max jobs claimed per call (1-100) and the time after which no new job is
# started (1000-50000 ms). A started job always finishes.
RECONCILIATION_DRAIN_MAX_JOBS=25
RECONCILIATION_DRAIN_BUDGET_MS=20000

# --- ScholarXIV Papers API (optional, M5.1 governance copilot) -------------
# [server] Read in src/lib/governance/scholarxiv.ts.
# The /governance copilot works without these: its recommendations and the
# citation chips come from a bundled list built from the README's references.
# With both set, a signed-in treasurer's copilot also checks each bundled paper
# against the ScholarXIV Papers search and marks it "confirmed" or
# "not found". It never invents a confirmation: a missing key, a timeout, or an
# unexpected response leaves the bundled list in place and says why.
#
# Docs: https://www.scholarxiv.com/developers
# Key:  minted in the ScholarXIV developer dashboard (starts with `sxv_`)
#
# This is a SERVER-SIDE credential. Never expose it as NEXT_PUBLIC_* and never
# call ScholarXIV from a browser.
#
# Base URL of the Papers API, without the trailing `/papers/search`. Must be
# https (http is accepted for localhost only). The documented search endpoint
# is `POST /api/v1/papers/search`, so this is normally:
#   https://www.scholarxiv.com/api/v1
SCHOLARXIV_API_URL=
SCHOLARXIV_API_KEY=

# Hard ceiling on each ScholarXIV call, in ms (500-30000). Default 8000.
SCHOLARXIV_TIMEOUT_MS=8000

# --- Addis AI (optional, Amharic voice entry: STT and TTS) -----------------
# [server] Read in src/lib/voice/addisAi.ts (via stt.ts and tts.ts).
# Addis AI is the Amharic server lane. Voxide is a separate thing: the English
# voice assistant, a client-side widget (its own variable lives elsewhere).
# Voice still works without these: browsers with on-device speech recognition
# and speechSynthesis need no key. Server transcription (/api/voice/transcribe)
# and audio digests (/api/voice/speak) need ADDIS_AI_API_KEY. With none, those
# routes answer 503 not-configured and never fabricate a result. Check with
# `GET /api/voice/capabilities`.
#
# This is a SERVER-SIDE credential. Never expose it as NEXT_PUBLIC_*.
# STT limits: 60 seconds and 10 MB per clip. Amharic only (no Oromo STT code).
# Docs: https://docs.addisassistant.com
# ADDIS_AI_API_KEY=

# Optional. Voice for audio digests. Default am-hamen. A plain id such as
# am-hamen (two letters, a dash, lowercase letters/digits/dashes); anything else
# leaves audio digests unconfigured.
# ADDIS_AI_TTS_VOICE=

# Optional. Which implementation serves each direction. Unset (or "addis-ai")
# means Addis AI; any other value disables that direction, so a typo fails closed.
# VOICE_STT_PROVIDER=
# VOICE_TTS_PROVIDER=

# --- Voxide voice assistant (browser widget) ----------------------------
# A publishable key (vox_pub_...) from the Voxide dashboard. Unlike the
# Addis AI secret above, THIS ONE IS MEANT FOR THE BROWSER: it is safe
# to expose as NEXT_PUBLIC_*, and it only works on the domains whitelisted in
# the Voxide dashboard (localhost always works). Add the live URL there.
# Left empty, the assistant is simply not shown and the app runs as before.
# Set it in .env.local or the host environment, and rebuild: NEXT_PUBLIC_*
# values are inlined at build time.
NEXT_PUBLIC_VOXIDE_KEY=

# --- Platform / tooling (not secrets; usually not set in this file) --------
# PORT      [server] Port the standalone Next server listens on. The Dockerfile
#           sets 3000; most container hosts inject their own. Read by Next and
#           by the Dockerfile HEALTHCHECK.
# HOSTNAME  [server] Bind address. The Dockerfile sets 0.0.0.0.
# NODE_ENV  Set by `next build`/`next start` and the Dockerfile (production).
#           The banking code refuses its in-memory stores and test adapters
#           outside development/test, so never run production with another
#           value.
# CI        Read only by playwright.config.ts (retries, workers, forbidOnly).
